# TPV with the radial terms of every degree the convention defines
# (PV_3 = r, PV_11 = r^3, PV_23 = r^5, PV_39 = r^7) on BOTH axes, plus
# constant, linear, quadratic and cubic terms and a rotated CD matrix.
# Synthetic, coefficients chosen to give ~0.1-10 arcsec corrections over a
# 0.15 x 0.3 deg chip (DECam/SCAMP-like scale), verified by wcslib.
# TOL_PX 1e-8: the s2p input is wcslib's p2s sky position, whose angular
# round-off (~2e-10 arcsec, the p2s budget measured on every case) is
# 8e-10 px at this case's 0.26 arcsec/px plate scale; measured Go vs wcslib
# max 1.1e-9 px. Known SIP/TPV inverse bugs were >= 1e-4 px.
TOL_PX 1e-8
NOTE pipeline: TPV radial terms r, r^3, r^5, r^7 on both axes (CD form)
GRID 1 2048 9 1 4096 9
PIX 1024.5 2048.5
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 2048
NAXIS2  = 4096
CTYPE1  = 'RA---TPV'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--TPV'
CRVAL1  = 35.5
CRVAL2  = -4.75
CRPIX1  = 1024.5
CRPIX2  = 2048.5
CD1_1   = 7.3E-05
CD1_2   = 1.1E-07
CD2_1   = -1.2E-07
CD2_2   = 7.3E-05
PV1_0   = 1.2E-05
PV1_1   = 1.0012
PV1_2   = -2.1E-03
PV1_3   = 1.0E-04
PV1_4   = 3.0E-03
PV1_5   = -2.2E-03
PV1_6   = 1.1E-03
PV1_7   = -1.0E-02
PV1_8   = 4.0E-03
PV1_9   = -9.0E-03
PV1_10  = 2.0E-03
PV1_11  = 5.0E-03
PV1_23  = 2.0E-02
PV1_39  = -3.0E-02
PV2_0   = -3.0E-05
PV2_1   = 1.0008
PV2_2   = 1.7E-03
PV2_3   = -2.0E-04
PV2_4   = 2.5E-03
PV2_5   = 1.8E-03
PV2_6   = -1.2E-03
PV2_7   = 7.0E-03
PV2_8   = -5.0E-03
PV2_9   = 3.0E-03
PV2_10  = -8.0E-03
PV2_11  = -4.0E-03
PV2_23  = 1.5E-02
PV2_39  = 4.0E-02
